{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Chiron","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chiron is a minor planet (centaur) orbiting between Saturn and Uranus."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Since Astronomy Engine doesn’t include Chiron as a built-in body,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions are calculated using gravity simulation with pre-computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state vectors from JPL Horizons."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chiron’s position is computed by:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Selecting the nearest reference epoch to the requested time"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializing a gravity simulation at that epoch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Propagating to the requested time"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Converting to the desired coordinate system"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Accuracy","level":2,"text":"Accuracy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Accuracy is highest near the reference epochs (2000, 2010, 2020, 2030, 2040)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and degrades slightly as distance from these epochs increases due to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numerical integration error. For typical usage within ±5 years of an epoch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error is expected to be less than 1 arcminute."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calculations are supported for years 1900 through 2150. Integration error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grows with distance from the reference epochs, so times outside this range"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throw "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError\/badTime"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Get Chiron's ecliptic longitude","let longitude = try Chiron.eclipticLongitude(at: .now)","print(\"Chiron is at \\(longitude)°\")","","\/\/ Get Chiron's geocentric position","let position = try Chiron.geocentricPosition(at: .now)","print(\"Chiron position: \\(position)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/chiron"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Provides position calculations for 2060 Chiron."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Chiron"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Advanced","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AdvancedFeatures","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/FixedStar","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GravitySimulation","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/LagrangePoint","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/LagrangePointID","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Jupiter","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/JupiterMoons","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/RotationAxis","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Atmosphere"],"anchor":"Advanced","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":[